hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4899","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Keep the original property with you and give its produce (in the way of Allah). Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) specified it for the needy, travelers, those striving in the way of Allah, slaves, and the poor. He gave the supervisor of the property the right to eat from it himself and to feed others from it, as long as he was not accumulating wealth from it."
"4900","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Give it as charity, such that you distribute its produce and keep the land itself with you, which cannot be sold nor gifted."
"4901","'Umar got some land in Khaibar, and when to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have acquired land in Khaibar which I consider to be more valuable than any I have acquired ; so what do you command me to do with it ? He replied: If you wish, you may make the property as inalienable possession, and give its produce as sadaqah (charity). So 'Umar gave it as a sadaqah declaring that the property must not be sold, given away, or inherited : (and gave its produce as sadaqah to be devoted) to poor, relatives, the emancipation of slaves, Allah's path, travellers. The narrator Bishr added: ""and guests"". Then the agreed version goes: No sin being committed by the one who administers it if he eats something from it in a reasonable manner, or gives something to a friend, who does not make his own property. The narrator Bishr added: ""(provided) he is not storing-up goods (for himself)"". (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2878)"
"4902","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""After a person dies, among the things he leaves behind, three are the best: righteous children who pray for him, ongoing charity whose reward continues to reach him, and good deeds that continue to be acted upon after him."
"4903","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the servant who is gentle when selling, gentle when buying, gentle when demanding (his due), and gentle when paying."
"4904","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The two parties to a transaction have the choice so long as they have not separated. If they are honest and open, their transaction will be blessed, but if they tell lies and conceal anything, the blessing of their transaction will be lost."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4457)"
"4905","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a heap of grain. He inserted his fingers into it and felt dampness. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O owner of this grain, what is this? He replied: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Rain had fallen on it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Why did you not put this (damp part) on top so that people could see it? Whoever deceives us is not from us."
"4906","""Taking oaths may help you to make a sale but it takes (blessing) away from the earnings ""(Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4461)"
"4907","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: There are three to whom Allah will not speak and at whom He will not look on the Day of Resurrection, and whom He will not declare pure, and they will have a painful punishment. I asked: Who are they, Messenger of Allah, they are losers and disappointed ? He repeated it three times. I asked: Who are they. Messenger of Allah, they are losers and disappointed ? He replied: The one who wears a trailing robe, the one who takes account of what he gives, and the one who produces a ready sale of a commodity by false swearing. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4087)"
"4908","I withhold My bounty from you, just as you withheld that surplus which was not the earning of your own hands."
"4909","I said, ""Will you sell this to me for three dirhams?"" He said, ""No, by Allah (I will not do so)."" Then he sold me the goat. Later, I mentioned this matter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) said: ""He has sold his Hereafter for his worldly life."
"4910","From his father, from his grandfather, that he went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the Musalla, and he saw the people doing business so he said: 'O people of trade!' and they replied to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turning their necks and their gazes towards him, and he said: Indeed the merchants will be resurrected on the Day of judgement with the wicked, except the one who has Taqwa of Allah, who behaves charitably and is truthful.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1210)"
"4911","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, you sell it to me. I replied: No, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! It is already yours. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, you sell it to me. I said: I owe a man one uqiyah of gold, so in exchange for that, it is yours. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I have taken it; you ride it until you reach Madinah. When I reached Madinah, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him): Give him one uqiyah of gold and pay him extra. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He gave me one uqiyah of gold and one qirat extra. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: So I resolved that the extra payment given by the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would never be separated from me. That amount remained safe with me in a pouch, then at the incident of Harrah, the people of Shaam took it away."
"4912","”The two parties to a transaction have the choice (of annulling it) so long as they have not yet parted."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2182)"
"4913","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""No deal is settled and finalized unless the buyer and the seller separate, except if the deal is optional (whereby the validity of the bargain depends on the stipulations agreed upon). (Using translation from Bukhārī 2113)"
"4914","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""When a person buys something, it becomes binding upon him, and he has the right regarding it over his companion until he separates from him. If he wishes, he may take it, and if he wishes, he may leave it. But if he separates from his companion, then he will no longer have any choice.\"""""
"4916","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Both the buyer and the seller have the option of canceling or confirming a bargain unless they separate, or the sale is optional."" (See Hadith No.320). (Using translation from Bukhārī 2111)"
"4917","""When two men enter into a transaction, each of them has the choice (of annulling it) so long as they have not yet parted and are still together, or one of them has given the option or choice to the other. Once he has accepted the terms of the other, then the transaction is binding. If they part after concluding the transaction and neither of them has rescinded the transaction then the transaction is binding.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2181)"
"4918","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Measure your food, may you be blessed therein.""' (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2231)"
"4919","""When the Prophet ﷺ came to Al-Madinah, they were the worst people in weights and measures. Then Allah, Glorious is He revealed: ""Woe to the Mutaffifun (those who give less in measure and weight)"",[1] and they were fair in weights and measures after that. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2223)"
"4920","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in this when you receive payment according to the value of that day, and both of you (parties) separate in such a state that there is no (condition of deferred payment) between you."
"4921","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a date-palm tree after it has been pollinated, and does not stipulate (at the time of transaction) a condition regarding its fruit, then he will get nothing of it. And whoever buys a slave and does not stipulate a condition regarding the wealth he possesses, then he will get nothing of it."
"4922","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: If anyone buys a slave who possesses property. his property belongs to the seller unless buyer makes a provision and if anyone buys palm-trees after they have been fecundated, the fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer make a provision. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3433)"
"4923","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: If anyone buys a slave who possesses property. his property belongs to the seller unless buyer makes a provision and if anyone buys palm-trees after they have been fecundated, the fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer make a provision. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3433)"
"4924","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever sells a slave who possesses some wealth, then that wealth will go to the seller, and if that slave has taken some debt, then its payment will be upon the seller, except if the buyer has stipulated a condition (then the ruling will be different). And whoever grafts a date-palm tree and, after grafting, sells it, then the fruit of that tree will go to the seller, except if the buyer has stipulated a condition (then the ruling will be different)."
"4925","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to them: Whoever does a forward sale should do so with specified measure and specified weight. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Minhal is Abdul Rahman bin Mut’im."
"4926","I asked: Did you do it with the person who owned fields or with the one who did not own fields? He replied: We did not investigate about this. (i.e., we used to conduct Salam transactions with both types of people)"",""He said: “Yes. We used to obtain war-booty in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"",""and we would pay in advance for wheat"","" barley"","" dates"","" and raisins.”"",""I said: “From someone who has crops"",""or from someone who does not have crops?”"",He said: “We did not used to ask them about that.”"
"4927","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Profit follows responsibility. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3508)"
"4928","narrator says: I went to Hisham and told him about this, so he returned the slave but did not return the kharaj."
"4929","the Prophet sold a Mudabbar. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4654)"
"4930","The Prophet (peace be upon him) gave this amount to that man. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He was a Coptic slave who died within a year."
"4931","The people replied, ""No."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Who will buy this slave from me?"" So Sayyiduna Na’eem Nahham (may Allah be pleased with him) bought him for eight hundred dirhams. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Spend this amount on yourself, and if anything remains, spend it on your relatives. If anything still remains, then spend it here and there (i.e., in the way of Allah)."
"4932","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sold that slave and said: When a person is in need, he should begin (spending) on himself. If he has something extra, he should spend on his wife and children, and if there is still something extra, he should spend on his close relatives."
"4933","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of him and sold him. He said: You are more in need of his price, and Allah is more free of need than this."
"4934","The name of this slave was Yaqub. And the person who freed him was named Abu Mazkur. That person had no wealth other than this slave. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called for the slave and inquired. He said, ""Who will buy him from me?"" So Sayyiduna Nu'aym bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who belonged to Banu 'Adi bin Ka'b, bought the slave from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for eight hundred dirhams. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called that person and said, ""When you are poor, begin with yourself. If you have surplus wealth, spend it on your wife and children. If there is still surplus, spend it on your relatives. If there is still surplus, then spend it here and there (i.e., in the way of Allah)."" The narrator states: Whenever Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith, he would also say: He was a Coptic slave who died within a year."
"4935","The people said: Messenger of Allah , prices have shot up, so fix prices for us. Thereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah is the one Who fixes prices, Who withholds, gives lavishly and provides, and I hope that when I meet Allah, none of you will have any claim on me for an injustice regarding blood or property. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3451)"
"4936","""No one hoards but a sinner.""' (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2154)"
"4937","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews. Allah made fat unlawful for them, so they melted it and then sold it and consumed its price."
"4938","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards the sky and then said: ""May Allah destroy the Jews; fat was made unlawful for them, so they sold it and began to consume its price. Indeed, when Allah declares something unlawful, He also declares its price unlawful."
"4939","The Prophet ﷺ forbade payment for dog and cat. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3479)"
"4940","I asked Jabir about the price of a dog and a cat; he said: Messenger of Allah ﷺ disapproved of that. (Using translation from Muslim 1569)"
"4941","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, the earnings of a prostitute, the price of a dog, the price of a cat, and the earnings of a cupper are forbidden."
"4942","""A man gave the Messenger of Allah a skin full of wine, and the Prophet said to him;' did you know that Allah has forbidden it?' He whispered something and I did not understand what he whispered as I wanted to. I asked a person who was beside him and the Prophet said to him; 'What are you whispering about?' He said: 'I told him to sell it.' The Prophet said: 'The One Who forbade drinking it also forbade selling it.' Then he opened the vessels and poured out their contents. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4664)"
"4943","“When the Verses at the end of Surat Al-Baqarah concerning usury were revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and forbade dealing in wine.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3382)"
"4944","I wish to present to you as a gift."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Do you know that Allah Almighty has declared it unlawful?"" He replied, ""No."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has declared it unlawful."" So the man turned to the person leading the camel and spoke to him in a low voice. That person stood up. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""What did you say to him?"" He replied, ""I instructed him to sell it."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Indeed, whatever has been declared unlawful to drink has also been declared unlawful to sell."" The narrator says: So the man ordered, and the mouth of the waterskin was opened, and the alcohol flowed out and mixed with the earth. I was watching it in the open field until nothing remained in that waterskin."
"4945","I was serving wine to eleven men. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (When the command of its prohibition reached them) those people instructed me to pour out that wine. People poured out the wine that was in their vessels, to the extent that it became difficult to pass through the streets because of the smell of that wine. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In those days, wine was made only from dried and fresh dates. A man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: I have the wealth of an orphan. I have bought wine with it. What is your opinion? Should I sell it and return the orphan’s wealth to him? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews. When fat was made unlawful for them, they sold it and consumed its price. (The narrator says) So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not permit me to sell the wine."
"4946","It was narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling the offspring of the offspring that is still in the womb of a camel. (Using translation from Aḥmad 394)"
"4947","the Messenger of Allah forbade selling the offspring of the offspring of a pregnant animal (Habal Al-Habalah), which was a transaction practiced by the people of the Jahiliyyah, whereby a man would buy camel to slaughter, but he would wait until the she-camel had produced offspring and the offspring in her belly had then produced offspring. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4625)"
"4948","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling or giving away the right to inheritance by a manumitted slave. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2919)"
"4949","The Prophet ﷺ forbade the selling of the Wala' (of slaves) or giving it as a present. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6756)"
"4950","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wala' is a firm bond like a blood relationship, which cannot be sold nor given as a gift."
"4951","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade Gharar transactions. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2195)"
"4952","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade the selling of water. The narrator named Amr did not know which type of water was meant by this."
"4953","That the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Do not withhold surplus water so that it is prevented from the pasture."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1272)"
"4954","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Do not withhold the superfluous water, for that will prevent people from grazing their cattle."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2353)"
"4955","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade the use of water from a well called ""Naq‘"" (forbidden to be used). (The narrator says:) By this is meant surplus water. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The mother of the narrator Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman is Amrah bint Abdur Rahman bin Sa‘d bin Zurara. This lady is the most knowledgeable woman regarding the narrations transmitted from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"4956","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Do not withhold surplus water and do not withhold grass, otherwise wealth (i.e., agricultural land) will perish and children will remain hungry."
"4957","This hadith has been reported on the authority of Jabir b. 'Abdullah through another chain of transmitters. (Using translation from Muslim 2116b)"
"4958","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade meeting traders on the way."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2179)"
"4959","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade meeting traders (outside the market) until they reach the market."
"4960","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'A town-dweller should not sell for a direst-dweller. Leave the people alone and let Allah provide for them from one another."""" (Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4495)"
"4961","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports this about the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He forbade meeting traders (to buy goods) outside the market, and he forbade that any city dweller should sell goods on behalf of a villager."
"4962","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade that any townsman should make a deal on behalf of a villager. He (peace be upon him) said: Do not meet the traders (outside the market)."
"4963","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: A townsman must not sell for a man from the desert ; and leave people alone, Allah will give them provision from one another. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3442)"
"4964","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: A townsman must not sell for a man from the desert ; and leave people alone, Allah will give them provision from one another. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3442)"
"4965","""Let one of you not undersell another.""[1] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2171)"
"4966","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""No person should make a deal over the deal of his brother, except with his permission."
"4967","I will never present myself before Allah in such a state that I have given someone’s wealth to another against his will. Buying and selling is done with mutual consent, however, there are some things in your transactions regarding which I want to advise you: do not bear malice against one another. Do not bid against each other. Do not be envious of one another, and no one should bid over his brother’s bid, and a townsman should never sell (anything) for a villager. Buying and selling is done with mutual consent. You are Allah’s servants and should live as brothers."
"4968","the Prophet ﷺ forbade the Najsh. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2173)"
"4969","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If any one of you sells a sheep or a milch- camel, let him not refrain from milking it.'' (Sahih ) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4486)"
"4970","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Do not go out to meet riders to conduct business with them ; none of you must buy in opposition to one another; and do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep, for he who buys them after that has been done has two courses open to him after milking them: he may keep them if he is pleased with them, or he may return them along with a sa' of dates is he is displeased with them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3443)"
"4971","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muzabanah, muhaqalah and thunya except it is known. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3405)"
"4972","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade Gharar transactions. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2195)"
"4973","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports regarding the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): He forbade two transactions in one transaction."
"4974","The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone makes two transactions combined in one bargain, he should have the lesser of the two or it will involve usury. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3461)"
"4975","the Messenger of Allah forbade Mulamash and Munabadha. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4509)"
"4976","""The Messenger of Allah forbade two kinds of garments and two kinds of transactions. As for the two kinds of transactions, they are Mulamash and Munabadhaha. Munabadha is when a man says, 'I throw this garment, and the transaction becomes binding, and Mulamasah is when a man touches it with his had, without spreading it out and checking it, and once he touches it, the transaction becomes binding."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4515)"
"4977","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade Gharar transaction sand Hasah transactions. "" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2194)"
"4978","He who buys foodgrain should not sell that before taking possession of it. He (the narrator) said: We used to buy foodgrain from the caravans in bulk, but Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to re-sell that until we had shifted it to some other place. (Using translation from Muslim 1526b)"
"4979","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""He who buys foodstuff should not sell it till he has received it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2133)"
"4980","He who buys food-rain should not sell it until he has taken possession of it. Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) said: I regard everything like food (so far as this principle is concerned). (Using translation from Muslim 1525c)"
"4981","Do not buy fruits (on the trees) until their good condition becomes clear. (Using translation from Muslim 1534g)"
"4982","""We used to buy food from troops of riders (i.e., the caravans) without knowing the amount, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to sell it until it had been delivered to us."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2229)"
"4983","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""O my nephew! When you buy something, do not sell it further until you have taken possession of it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration is famous as being transmitted from Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) through Yusuf bin Malik. In this, there is no mention of the narrator named Abdullah bin Ismah, and this narration is ""gharib"" (rare/isolated)."
"4984","I also participated in the bidding until I bought that oil from him. Then a man came to me and started offering me a higher price until he satisfied me. I was about to strike my hand with his (i.e., finalize the deal) when suddenly someone grabbed my wrist from behind. I turned around and saw that it was Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). He said to me: ""Do not sell it until you have transferred it to your specific place, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this."" (Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, says) So I withheld my hand."
"4985","I bought some grain from the charity grain. Before taking possession of it, I started getting profit from it. I intended to sell it. I asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about this, so he said: Do not sell it until you have taken possession of it."
"4986","The narrator states: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a person from selling it before transferring it to another place. (The narrator is unsure about one word here.)"
"4987","I saw that in the blessed era of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), those grain dealers were beaten who, after buying grain by estimation, would sell it to others before transferring it to their own designated place."
"4988","""the Messenger of Allah forbade selling the fruit of date palms until they are fit to eat."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4525)"
"4989","""Do not sell fruits until they have ripened.""' (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2215)"
"4990","the Messenger of Allah forbade selling fruits before they ripen. It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah what does ripen mean?"" he said: 'when they turn red."" And the Messenger of Allah said: ""What do you think if Allah withholds the fruits (causes it not to ripen), why would any one of you take his brother's wealth?"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4526)"
"4991","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fruits till they were clearly in good condition, forbidding it both to the seller and to the buyer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3367)"
"4992","I asked Ata bin Abi Rabah, ""Did you yourself hear Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Yes."" The Sheikh says: This narrator named Abu Walid is Saeed bin Mina, from whom Imam Abu Hanifa (may Allah have mercy on him) has narrated traditions."
"4993","The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of grapes till they became black and the sale of grain till it had become hard. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3371)"
"4994","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling palm-trees till the dates began to ripen, and ears of corn till they were white and were safe from blight, forbidding it both to the buyer and to the seller. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3368)"
"4995","the Prophet ﷺ forbade the deal involving earnest money . (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2192)"
"4996","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the Muhaqalah and the Muzabanah. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2266)"
"4997","The people replied: “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Then it will not be allowed (i.e., this is not permissible).” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant by this is: selling fresh barley in exchange for dry barley."
"4998","Ibn Umar (Allah be pleased them) reported Messenger of Allah ﷺ having forbidden Muzabana, and Muzabana implies the selling of fresh dates for dry dates by measuring them out and the selling of raisins by measure for grapes. (Using translation from Muslim 1542a)"
"4999","The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of fruits on the tree for fruits by measure, and sale of grapes for raisins by measure, and sale of harvest for wheat by measure. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3361)"
"5000","From Jabir that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited Al-Muhaqalah, Al-Muzabanah, Al-Mukhabarah, and Al-Mu'awamah, and he permitted it in the case of Al-'Araya. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1313)"
"5001","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) granted concession to the owner of ‘Ariyyah; he can sell dates by estimation."
"5002","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit in exchange for fruit, except that he permitted ‘Ariyyah, which c"
"5003","Which of them is better? He replied: Soft and white kind of wheat. So he forbade him from it and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (sawa) say, when he was asked about buying dry dates for fresh. The Messenger of Allah (sawa) said: Are fresh dates diminished when they become dry? The (the people) replied: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. Abu Dawud said: A similar tradition has also been transmitted by Isma'il b. Umayyah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3359)"
"5004","""Zaid bin Thabit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a concession regarding the sale of 'Araya.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2268)"
"5005","narrates from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): He permitted the sale of ‘Araya based on estimation."
"5006","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted Al-'Araya in cases less than five Wasq. Or similar. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1301)"
"5007","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted Al-'Araya in cases less than five Wasq. Or similar. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1301)"
"5008","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: (It can be sold) when it is one wasq or two wasqs, or three or four."
"5009","""The Messenger of Allah granted a concession allowing 'Araya sales for fresh dates and for dried dates, but he did not allow anything other than that."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4540)"
"5010","The reason is that when Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) made this sword for ‘As bin Wa’il, at that time Allah had not revealed the verse regarding the command of fighting, nor had jihad been made obligatory. The reason is that the obligation of jihad and the command to fight the polytheists was revealed after the Prophet (peace be upon him) left Makkah, as we have mentioned earlier, and this incident of Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) is from Makkah, which is before Allah made jihad obligatory upon the people."
"5011","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “When exchanging grain for grain, it must be equal.” And in those days, our grain was barley."
"5012","""Dinar for Dinar Dirham for Dirham, no difference between them."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4567)"
"5013","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said ­- and on one occasion Sufyan said: ['Umar] heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say ­ “Gold for silver is riba unless it is exchanged on the spot [lit. ‘this for that'), wheat for wheat is riba unless it is exchanged on the spot, barley for barley is riba unless it is exchanged on the spot, dates for dates is riba unless it is exchanged on the spot.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 162)"
